      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:14 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Benjamin Horwich",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1569",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45234a80b97f23460e4342e7966e7e6b9c86852dfe5dcde59f263496e3906b23",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45234a80b97f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HORWICH: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Section 924(c)(1) starts by defining a single crime of using or carrying a firearm during and in relation to a crime of violence or a drug trafficking crime."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1569",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45234a80b97f23460e4342e7966e7e6b9c86852dfe5dcde59f263496e3906b23",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45234a80b97f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Does the government believe that it has sufficiently argued this, or would you suggest on the government's behalf that if it becomes an issue it's set for reargument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1569",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45234a80b97f23460e4342e7966e7e6b9c86852dfe5dcde59f263496e3906b23",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45234a80b97f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondents have offered nothing in the way of a justification for overruling Harris."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1569",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45234a80b97f23460e4342e7966e7e6b9c86852dfe5dcde59f263496e3906b23",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45234a80b97f-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The government cannot point to a single defendant under this provision for the conduct at issue who has ever received more than 10 years in prison absent the use of a machinegun."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1569",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45234a80b97f23460e4342e7966e7e6b9c86852dfe5dcde59f263496e3906b23",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45234a80b97f-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So the question I have for you is: How do we find substantive unreasonableness?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1569",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "45234a80b97f23460e4342e7966e7e6b9c86852dfe5dcde59f263496e3906b23",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45234a80b97f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't contend that Castillo absolutely decides the case. My contention that I was trying to make is that when this Court looks to tradition for purposes of construing the new amendments, that Castillo gives the answer on -- at least on tradition, at least as applying that particular question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1569",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "45234a80b97f23460e4342e7966e7e6b9c86852dfe5dcde59f263496e3906b23",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45234a80b97f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The prior statute -- which was 18 U.S.C. 924(c)(1), right? That did deal with short-barreled rifle, short-barreled shotgun, machinegun, and so forth, but that's -- that provision didn't say anything about brandishing or discharge."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1569",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "45234a80b97f23460e4342e7966e7e6b9c86852dfe5dcde59f263496e3906b23",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45234a80b97f-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It's a collateral point: Does the government have to show, or does the -- don't you have to find that the machinegun is operable?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1569",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "45234a80b97f23460e4342e7966e7e6b9c86852dfe5dcde59f263496e3906b23",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45234a80b97f-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "has to prove knowledge. And we do emphasize that that would be an alternative basis for this Court to decide this case, by saying you at least have to prove knowledge even if it\u2019s a sentencing factor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1569",
